# Cloudflare D1: JSON body + generated columns

## Which database

| Database | Holds | Tenancy |
|----------|--------|---------|
| **Shared D1** | `customers`, `workers`, `providers` | Platform-wide; one instance for all tenants |
| **Worker D1** | `users`, `groups`, `clients`, `cases`, `documents`, contacts, … | **One D1 per deployed worker environment**; provisioned when the worker is created |

Customer data never shares a D1 across workers. 

## Row pattern (worker D1 entities)

- Store the full record in `body TEXT NOT NULL` (JSON string).
- Only create “real” columns for fields you query/filter/sort/index.
- Expose those fields as `GENERATED ALWAYS AS (json_extract(body, '$.…')) STORED`.
- Add indexes on generated columns you query frequently.
- Use `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT` for surrogate ids unless you have a strong reason not to.

Shared D1 tables (`customers`, `workers`, `providers`) may use relational columns where appropriate; they do not use the document `body` pattern unless you explicitly choose it.

## Example (worker D1 — `clients`)

```sql
CREATE TABLE clients (
  client_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,

  body TEXT NOT NULL,

  client_type TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (json_extract(body, '$.client_type')) STORED,
  last_name TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (json_extract(body, '$.last_name')) STORED,
  is_deleted INTEGER GENERATED ALWAYS AS (json_extract(body, '$.is_deleted')) STORED
);

CREATE INDEX idx_clients_deleted ON clients(is_deleted);
CREATE INDEX idx_clients_type ON clients(client_type);
```

Tracking fields (`version`, `updated_at`, etc.) live **inside** `body` unless you promote them to generated columns for indexing.
